63,3,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
64,3,,status,Servas,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
65,3,1,talk,Shion,,Option A is a disaster waiting to happen. We already have crumbs in our keyboards; giving people a dedicated place to make a mess without a professional cleaning plan just invites more chaos to spill into the office.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm not sure. Option A would stop the crumbs at the desks, but the cost is 96,000 yen. However, Option B is even more expensive at 141,000 yen, though it might stop those outside hire invoices.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Rin,,"Option B sounds like a great idea! If we have a calendar, everyone knows when it's their turn and nobody has to fight over who gets there first! Plus, no more scary awkward talks in front of everyone!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Option B offers a structured way to meet, but we must ask ourselves: does a calendar foster connection, or merely manage it? We need a place where we can truly see and hear one another.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option A is a liability. ""Maintained by whoever uses them"" is a vague promise that inevitably results in a few people doing all the work while others leave the mess. It is a recipe for resentment and wasted hours.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Toshio, exactly. Option A is a fantasy of self-regulation. Between the noise of appliances and the inevitable filth, it would be a nightmare for those of us sitting right next to the door. We need a function that respects the office's peace.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Shion, I... I understand. But if we choose Option B, we can finally stop paying those outside hire fees. I'm just worried about who will be responsible for the 141,000 yen payment. It's a lot of money to sign for.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Daisuke, don't be scared of the big number! If we stop paying for those other rooms, it's like we're saving money in the long run! Plus, a calendar is like a game—everyone gets a fair turn!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, your joy is infectious. However, we must consider that a bookable room can become a wall between us. If we only meet by appointment, we lose the spontaneous warmth that turns colleagues into friends.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Servas, spontaneity is a luxury we cannot afford if it means inefficient use of space. Option B is the most rational choice; it replaces expensive outside hires with a controlled, bookable system that minimizes unplanned labor.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Toshio, for once, your logic is sound. Option B is the only choice that provides a boundary. A bookable space implies a level of professionalism and order that Option A lacks, and it's far more useful than a room for sitting in silence.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think I agree with Toshio and Shion. If we choose Option B, we can stop the monthly payments for outside rooms, which feels safer. I'm still a bit nervous about the cost, but it seems like the most responsible choice.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Daisuke, see? Everyone is starting to like it! Option B is the best because it's fair and organized. No more ""first come, first served"" fights or cleaning up after people who forgot! I'm voting for Option B!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, your enthusiasm is a gift. While I fear the loss of spontaneity, I recognize that we desperately need a sanctuary for the difficult conversations we currently avoid. If Option B provides the privacy we lack, it may finally allow us to truly know one another.","{""words"":46,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Servas, if the room is bookable, it ensures that the time spent there is intentional and the labor of managing it is systematized. It is the only option that eliminates financial waste and prevents an invisible labor drain. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Shion,,"Option B is the only logical conclusion. It solves the financial leak of outside hires and, more importantly, imposes a structure that prevents the room from becoming a source of noise and filth. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'll vote for Option B too. It's a big cost upfront, but stopping those outside hire invoices feels like the right thing to do for the budget. I'm glad we all agree. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Rin,,Yay! We all agree! Option B is the most fair and organized way to do it. No more fighting over the room or cleaning up mysteries! I'm so happy we found a solution! I vote for Option B!,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,Servas,,"It is a comfort to see us reach a consensus. While I long for the warmth of unplanned friendship, the need for a private space to speak our truths is paramount. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"The consensus is clear. Option B is the only choice that replaces financial waste with a structured system, ensuring that neither the budget nor the staff's time is drained by inefficiency. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
